<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan central bank takes 1,055 mln in fed bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan central bank takes 1,055 mln in fed bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank said on Wednesday it had accepted 1,055 million rupees in an open market operation in Short Term Federal Bonds.</p>
<p>			Offered     Accepted	Max cut-off</p>
<p> Outright sales   1,055	 1,055 1	 6.75 pct/yr</p>
<p> Five-month REPO  nil	   nil	     nil</p>
<p> Three-month REPO nil	   nil	     nil</p>
<p> One-month REPO   nil	   nil	     nil</p>
<p>Total(million rupees)1,055 1,055</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
